      "text": "Let's figure out what multiplying really means. Imagine you have three baskets, and each basket has four apples inside. Basket one has four, basket two has four, and basket three has four. Instead of counting every single apple, we can use multiplication. Three baskets times four apples in each equals twelve apples altogether. Three times four equals twelve. The times sign means groups of. Three groups of four. So when you see a times sign, think, \"How many groups? How many in each group?\" Now you know the secret of multiplying.",
